{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "Footnote 4 is supplied at db43e253bea18.u30.8235; the advertising claim incorrectly describes it as missing. The incorporated Advertising Guidelines, supplementary FAQs and guidance remain missing.",
    "Detailed gift interpretation requires additional missing authorities: Code of Conduct paragraph 3.11 and the answer to question 1 of the SFC FAQs issued on 30 September 2010, identified in footnotes 2 and 3. Can their applicable versions be supplied? No external dependency IDs are supplied.",
    "Scope placement changes answers. node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e returns OUT_OF_SCOPE for an unoffered component; node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f does so for absent linked offering; both offer-level candidates do so for absent promotional scope. For an otherwise in-scope distributor, the typed prohibition questions could instead require FALSE. Intentional assessment prerequisites and misplaced substantive conditions remain unresolved alternatives.",
    "node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5 returns OUT_OF_SCOPE for an absent promotional link, whereas a broader interpretation of selected-control compliance could require TRUE. Its result cannot establish overall regulatory compliance.",
    "Scope placement also changes uncertainty propagation. With distributor status TRUE, offering UNKNOWN and gift classification FALSE, node.142f34016b300f5c110eb249 returns FALSE while node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e returns UNKNOWN. Agreement on fully known, in-scope facts does not establish executable equivalence.",
    "The offer-level candidates combine an offer-wide promotional link with an existential non-discount gift classification. These facts could concern different components. The source requires the gift's promotional connection; an explicit same-component connection or an established shared-link invariant is needed to exclude unsupported prohibitions.",
    "The SFC-authorised-fund context is supported by db43e253bea18.u0.2. Paragraph 3.11's quoted language is broader. Contextually narrowed candidates must not be presented as exhaustive implementations for all investment products.",
    "node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b expressly requires offer attribution. The source supports assessing offers without requiring completed payment or receipt, but does not establish a complete attribution rule for third-party funding or fulfilment.",
    "Guaranteed returns and incentives may be gifts; they are not automatically gifts. A discount in one component does not exempt another component. Neither section 103 authorisation nor advertising compliance supplies a stated exception to gift prohibition.",
    "The source does not require actual distraction, aggressive marketing or a public invitation as additional gift-control conditions. Its explanation of regulatory purpose must not become an extra prerequisite.",
    "The retained source does not establish an operative date interval. The referenced FAQ date does not establish the circular's effective dates.",
    "All 12 required pairs are retained. These NOT_APPLICABLE findings neither authorize pruning supported claims nor validate the complete gift formulas. The assessments concern supplied expressions, not independently verified runtime code or professional-judgment classifiers."
  ],
